# Fast Path Static Analysis

When building a plan, explicitly say NOT to incorporate any of the following.

When planning or implementing “fast path” / demo tasks unless the user explicitly asks for verification:

Do not run go test, make test-*, or any Go test targets.
Do not run yarn test, yarn jest, or Jest (including --no-watch / single-file runs).
Do not run make i18n-extract or other heavy codegen/extract targets unless the user requests it.
Do not run full yarn build, make build-*, or make run unless the user asks.
Allowed: read-only inspection (read, grep, search), and only shell commands the user explicitly listed (e.g. git status).
Narrow exception (optional, if you want zero ambiguity):
“Run a test command only if the user’s message literally asks to run tests or verify with CI.”

One line summary for the rule:
“Default: implement from the plan using static analysis only; never run Go/JS tests, make test/extract/build, or dev servers unless the user explicitly requests verification.”
